tree-sitter-wasms ships prebuilt WebAssembly grammars. Each grammar keeps the license of
its own upstream project. Inventory below: the license field that the npm registry reports
for each upstream grammar package, looked up 21 Oct 2026. The wrapper build used earlier
grammar versions, so confirm each against the exact version before a public release.
This is an inventory, not legal advice.

  c, c_sharp, cpp, css, embedded_template, go, html, java, kotlin, lua, objc, ocaml, php,
  ruby, rust, scala, swift, systemrdl, toml, zig, tlaplus, bash, python, typescript,
  javascript, json, yaml, elm, ql, elisp ....................................... MIT
  elixir ............................................................... Apache-2.0
  dart, rescript, solidity, vue ..... built from GitHub sources, not npm. Check upstream:
    UserNobody14/tree-sitter-dart, rescript-lang/tree-sitter-rescript,
    JoranHonig/tree-sitter-solidity, tree-sitter-grammars/tree-sitter-vue.
  (Elisp, Elm and QL are present in the grammar bundle but not mapped to a file type.)

No WASM binaries or node_modules are included in this repository; npm installs them.
